---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, socials } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${site.shortName} measures website use without cookies or storing IP addresses.`}
>
  <section class="bg-brand-light/50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-6 sm:py-8">
      <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-brand-dark sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink sm:text-lg">
        We count how our website is used so we can see what’s helpful to the community and report on our work.
        We keep it simple, private and as anonymous as we can.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-6 pb-10 prose-headings:font-heading prose-headings:text-brand-dark prose-p:text-ink prose-li:text-ink prose-a:text-brand sm:pt-8 sm:pb-12">
    <h2>What we count</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Which pages are viewed, and on which day.</li>
      <li>The website that sent you here, reduced to its name (for example, facebook.com), or a campaign tag in the link you followed.</li>
      <li>Clicks on key links, such as our membership form, social media pages and documents.</li>
      <li>When the Protect a tree email builder is started, opened in an email app, or copied.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Unique visitors</h2>
    <p>
      To estimate how many different people visit each day, our server briefly combines your IP address and browser
      type into a temporary code. We don’t store your IP address. The code, and the secret used to create it, change
      every day and are deleted afterwards, so visits on different days can’t be linked. Our public “Protect a tree
      assists” tally uses the same kind of daily code to avoid counting repeat clicks.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don’t collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don’t use cookies or advertising trackers to measure visits.</li>
      <li>
        We don’t receive the answers you enter in our email builder, including tree addresses, names, contact details
        or email text. Your draft is created in your browser. We only see your email if you choose to copy us into it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who can see it and for how long</h2>
    <p>
      Only committee members with an approved login can view the figures, which are daily totals rather than records
      about individuals. We keep daily totals for about 13 months.
    </p>

    <h2>Choosing not to be counted</h2>
    <p>
      If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or “Do Not Track” signal, we don’t count your visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Services we use</h2>
    <p>
      Our website is hosted by Netlify, which processes standard technical information, such as IP addresses, to
      deliver and secure the site. Our font is loaded from Google Fonts, which also receives your IP address when the
      page loads.
    </p>

    {socials.email && (
      <>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Email us at <a href={`mailto:${socials.email}`}>{socials.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </>
    )}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
